<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cheonghaejin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">828–851</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cheonghaejin was a maritime garrison founded in 828 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jang-bogo">Jang Bogo</a>, with royal permission, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wando">Wando</a> island off the south-western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. From it Jang Bogo suppressed piracy and controlled trade between Silla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. After his assassination the garrison was abolished in 851 and its people moved inland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cheonghaejin.jpg" alt="Cheonghaejin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: hyolee2 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wando_Jang-do.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
